-- תקנון שירות עובדי הוראה, פרק 1א', §1.6 קצובת ביגוד
-- The clothing allowance: who is entitled, its level by seniority, how it
-- is pro-rated, when it is paid, and how it sits beside other clothing
-- arrangements.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common
IMPORT conventions

§ `1.6 קצובת ביגוד`

@desc One school year of a teaching employee's service, as far as section 1.6 asks about it.
DECLARE `clothing year` HAS
    `ranked on the teaching employees' scale`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed in a teaching role`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `year of teaching seniority`               IS A NUMBER  @desc which year of teaching seniority this is, counting the year being served (F-1.6-a), before the compulsory-service years are taken out
    `years of compulsory army service counted in it` IS A NUMBER @desc years of compulsory IDF service included in that seniority (section 1.6.2, note 3)
    `position in each month worked`            IS A LIST OF NUMBER  @desc the share of a full position held in each month of the year the employee worked (1 = one full position); one entry where it did not change
    `share of the year worked`                 IS A NUMBER  @desc the extent of work in the year, as a share of the full year (1 = the whole year)
    `level 1 amount`                           IS A NUMBER  @desc the yearly amount at level 1 of the clothing allowance customary for public-facing civil servants (section 1.6.1), set by the Treasury and published by the conditions-of-service department (section 1.6.2); an input
    `level 2 amount`                           IS A NUMBER  @desc the yearly amount at level 2, set the same way; an input
    `clothing allowance under other arrangements` IS A NUMBER @desc any clothing allowance the employee receives under the arrangements section 1.6.4 keeps in force; an input

§§ `1.6.1`

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_6__hc_2__para_1
GIVEN y IS A `clothing year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to the clothing allowance` y IF
        y's `ranked on the teaching employees' scale`
    AND y's `employed in a teaching role`

§§ `1.6.2`

-- The levels AS PRINTED, as rows, so the table can be asked directly.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_6__hc_2__para_2 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_6__hc_2__para_2/p2 akn:chp_1א___sec_1_6__hc_2__para_2/p3
DECLARE `clothing band` HAS
    `band level`    IS A NUMBER
    `band from`     IS A NUMBER
    `band to`       IS A NUMBER  @desc 999 stands for "+", with no upper bound

`the clothing levels` MEANS
    LIST `clothing band` 1 1  25,
         `clothing band` 2 26 999

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
DECIDE `the levels the table gives for seniority` n IS
    map (GIVEN b YIELD b's `band level`)
        (filter (GIVEN b YIELD n AT LEAST b's `band from` AND n AT MOST b's `band to`)
                `the clothing levels`)

-- F-1.6-a: the reading adopted counts the year being served (the first year
-- is 1), as F-1.7-b does for the same words in §1.7; read as completed
-- years a teacher in the first year has seniority 0 and no level.
-- Convention thresholds.seniority (conventions.toml): "N years" are completed
-- years, but a table built on the year of seniority counts the year being
-- served, and §1.6.2 sets the level "לפי שנת ותק בהוראה".
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `clothing level` n IS
    IF n AT LEAST 26 THEN 2 ELSE 1

`a first-year teacher has no clothing level if seniority counts completed years` MEANS
    `the levels the table gives for seniority` 0 EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `a first-year teacher has no clothing level if seniority counts completed years`

-- The table gives every year from 1 to 40 exactly one level, the one adopted.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN n YIELD `the levels the table gives for seniority` n EQUALS LIST (`clothing level` n))
            (LIST 1, 2, 10, 24, 25, 26, 27, 40)

-- The note to §1.6.2: compulsory army service carries no right for the
-- allowance, so its years are taken out of the seniority the levels read.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_6__hc_2__para_2/p4
GIVEN y IS A `clothing year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `seniority for the clothing level` y IS
    y's `year of teaching seniority` MINUS y's `years of compulsory army service counted in it`

-- §1.6.2 ¶5: the Treasury sets the amounts and the department publishes them
-- yearly, so the amount of each level is an input of the year.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_6__hc_2__para_2/p5
GIVEN y IS A `clothing year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `level amount` y IS
    IF `clothing level` (`seniority for the clothing level` y) EQUALS 2
    THEN y's `level 2 amount`
    ELSE y's `level 1 amount`

§§ `1.6.3`

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_6__hc_2__para_3
GIVEN y IS A `clothing year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `clothing pro-rating` y IS
    `the year's position share` (y's `position in each month worked`) TIMES y's `share of the year worked`

-- F-1.6-b: "יחסית לשיעור המשרה, אך לא יותר ממשרה אחת" does not say how a
-- position that changes within the year is measured, nor whether the cap of
-- one position binds each month or the year as a whole. Convention
-- position.yearly: the mean of the months, each month up to one position.
-- Capping the year's mean instead pays more to a year of 1.2 and 0.6:
`a year of 1.2 then 0.6 is paid differently if one position caps the year` MEANS
    NOT (`the year's position share` (LIST 1.2, 1.2, 1.2, 1.2, 1.2, 0.6, 0.6, 0.6, 0.6, 0.6)
         EQUALS min ((1.2 TIMES 5 PLUS 0.6 TIMES 5) DIVIDED BY 10) 1)
#ASSERT `a year of 1.2 then 0.6 is paid differently if one position caps the year`

@export default The clothing allowance a teaching employee is owed for one year under section 1.6 of the takanon, before the allowance under other arrangements that section 1.6.4 adds to it
GIVEN y IS A `clothing year` @desc the employee's year
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `clothing allowance` y IS
    IF `entitled to the clothing allowance` y
    THEN `level amount` y TIMES `clothing pro-rating` y
    ELSE 0

§§ `1.6.4`

@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_6__hc_2__para_4
GIVEN y IS A `clothing year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `clothing allowances in all` y IS
    `clothing allowance` y PLUS y's `clothing allowance under other arrangements`

§§ `1.6.2 ¶6 Payment`

DECLARE `clothing action` IS ONE OF
    `pay the clothing allowance` HAS `amount paid out` IS A NUMBER

-- Time in school months (September = 1): July's salary is the eleventh.
@ref akn:chp_1א___sec_1_6__hc_2__para_2/p6
GIVEN y IS A `clothing year`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `clothing action`
DECIDE `payment with July's salary` y IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the clothing allowance` `amount paid out`
          PROVIDED `amount paid out` AT LEAST `clothing allowance` y
    WITHIN `month number` July
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "section 1.6.2: the allowance is paid with July's salary"

§§ `1.6.5–1.6.6`

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_6__hc_2__para_5 A pointer: the clothing allowance of physical-education teachers is in section 3.9.4.
-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_6__hc_2__para_6 A pointer: the clothing allowance of vocational instructors and של"ח instructors is in section 6.17.7.

-- Worked examples. The level amounts of 1,000 and 1,200 are placeholders:
-- the takanon leaves the amounts to the Treasury.
`a part-time teacher in year 28 with 3 army years` MEANS
    `clothing year` WITH
        `ranked on the teaching employees' scale`         IS TRUE
        `employed in a teaching role`                     IS TRUE
        `year of teaching seniority`                      IS 28
        `years of compulsory army service counted in it`  IS 3
        `position in each month worked`                   IS LIST 0.5
        `share of the year worked`                        IS 1
        `level 1 amount`                                  IS 1000
        `level 2 amount`                                  IS 1200
        `clothing allowance under other arrangements`     IS 0

-- 28 years less 3 army years is 25: level 1, half of 1,000.
#ASSERT `clothing allowance` `a part-time teacher in year 28 with 3 army years` EQUALS 500

#TRACE `payment with July's salary` `a part-time teacher in year 28 with 3 army years` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the clothing allowance` 500 AT 11

-- akn:chp_1א___sec_1_6__hc_3 The section's sources (אסמכתא): the circular, agreement and letter it rests on.

§§ `Property checks`

-- The section's rules over their whole finite space: every year of teaching
-- seniority from 1 to 50 with up to five army years counted in it (a year
-- of seniority always holds at least the year being served, so there are
-- fewer army years than the year's number), a grid of position fractions
-- and shares of the year, and both values of each eligibility condition.

`the seniority years checked` MEANS range 1 50
`the army years checked` MEANS range 0 5
`the shares checked` MEANS LIST 0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1, 1.25, 1.5

GIVEN p IS A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER AND NUMBER TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `holds for every seniority and army years` p IF
    all (GIVEN n YIELD
            all (GIVEN a YIELD a AT LEAST n OR p n a) `the army years checked`)
        `the seniority years checked`

-- Totality and exclusivity of the levels: once the army years are taken out,
-- the printed table gives every case exactly one level, and it is the level
-- the encoding pays.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, a IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the table gives the year exactly the level paid` n a IF
    `the levels the table gives for seniority` (n MINUS a) EQUALS LIST (`clothing level` (n MINUS a))

#ASSERT `holds for every seniority and army years` `the table gives the year exactly the level paid`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, a IS A NUMBER, position IS A NUMBER, share IS A NUMBER
      entitled IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `clothing year`
DECIDE `a checked clothing year` n a position share entitled IS
    `clothing year` WITH
        `ranked on the teaching employees' scale`         IS entitled
        `employed in a teaching role`                     IS TRUE
        `year of teaching seniority`                      IS n
        `years of compulsory army service counted in it`  IS a
        `position in each month worked`                   IS LIST position
        `share of the year worked`                        IS share
        `level 1 amount`                                  IS 1000
        `level 2 amount`                                  IS 1200
        `clothing allowance under other arrangements`     IS 300

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, a IS A NUMBER, p IS A FUNCTION FROM `clothing year` TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `holds at every position and share for` n a p IF
    all (GIVEN position YIELD
            all (GIVEN share YIELD
                    all (GIVEN entitled YIELD p (`a checked clothing year` n a position share entitled))
                        (LIST TRUE, FALSE))
                (filter (GIVEN s YIELD s AT MOST 1) `the shares checked`))
        `the shares checked`

-- Bounds (1.6.3): never negative, never more than the level's yearly amount
-- (no more than one position, and no more than the whole year), nothing
-- for an employee 1.6.1 does not entitle, and 1.6.4 only adds.
GIVEN y IS A `clothing year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the allowance is within its bounds` y IF
        `clothing allowance` y AT LEAST 0
    AND `clothing allowance` y AT MOST `level amount` y
    AND (`entitled to the clothing allowance` y OR `clothing allowance` y EQUALS 0)
    AND `clothing allowances in all` y AT LEAST `clothing allowance` y

#ASSERT `holds for every seniority and army years` (GIVEN n, a YIELD `holds at every position and share for` n a `the allowance is within its bounds`)

-- Monotonicity: more position (up to one) or more of the year never pays
-- less; past one position nothing more is paid.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, a IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a larger position or share never pays less` n a IF
    and (zipWith (GIVEN p, q YIELD
                        `clothing allowance` (`a checked clothing year` n a p 1 TRUE)
                        AT MOST `clothing allowance` (`a checked clothing year` n a q 1 TRUE)
                    AND `clothing allowance` (`a checked clothing year` n a 1 p TRUE)
                        AT MOST `clothing allowance` (`a checked clothing year` n a 1 q TRUE))
                 `the shares checked`
                 (drop 1 `the shares checked`))
    AND `clothing allowance` (`a checked clothing year` n a 1.5 1 TRUE)
        EQUALS `clothing allowance` (`a checked clothing year` n a 1 1 TRUE)

#ASSERT `holds for every seniority and army years` `a larger position or share never pays less`

-- Seniority: the level never goes back as the years grow, and an army year
-- never raises it. (Whether level 2 pays more than level 1 is the
-- Treasury's amount, not the text's; the levels themselves are what the
-- text orders.)
#ASSERT and (zipWith (GIVEN n, m YIELD `clothing level` n AT MOST `clothing level` m)
                     `the seniority years checked`
                     (drop 1 `the seniority years checked`))
#ASSERT `holds for every seniority and army years` (GIVEN n, a YIELD
                                                        `clothing level` (n MINUS a) AT MOST `clothing level` n)
